title escapes that name no file

# A backslash not followed by three octal digits is malformed rather
# than literal -- the one compatibility edge in the escaping change,
# since a lone backslash used to be a literal.
#
# NUL and '/' are the two bytes no file name may hold, so an escaped
# one must be REJECTED rather than smuggled past a check that ran on
# the spelling. That is why decoding happens before validation, and
# why the '/' complaint quotes the DECODED name: it names the actual
# problem rather than its spelling.
#
# The out-of-range case (\400 and up) is not here yet. It is in
# devcheck/pending/ until both parsers agree to reject it.

tree base
  1-1: /
    2-100: lone\slash
    3-100: has\000nul
    4-100: esc\057slash
